    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a condensed lineup, as core contributors like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** are unavailable due to team off-days, significantly thinning our depth. Consequently, **Sam Antonacci** emerges as our strongest play with a score of 63.61. Batting lead-off against Rocker, **Antonacci** benefits from a 10% boost for his high-leverage spot in the order and a favorable platoon advantage. While **Miguel Vargas** also faces Rocker in the same game, his score of 55.00 is tempered by a negative park adjustment; however, his 0.389 xwOBA suggests he remains a stable pivot if we need to chase base-knocks rather than pure power.\n\n**Nasim Nunez** earns a marginal start at 59.76, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Feltner (5.10 xERA). Despite batting ninth, which yields a -8% penalty, **Nunez** is our priority for SB accumulation; his high sprint speed remains the primary driver for his inclusion, as he provides the best opportunity to steal a category that is currently the scarcest in our 5x5 build. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** rounds out the starters at 51.66. His projection is dragged down by a tough matchup against Ashcraft (3.28 xERA), but a 13% boost for his platoon profile against a right-handed starter keeps him marginally ahead of the replacement level. We are holding reserves like **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** on the bench today, as the current projections indicate their situational scoring floors do not justify burning through our limited game caps while facing mid-tier arms.",
